WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.916 --> 00:00:31.416
<b>In chapter 5,</b>

2
00:00:31.416 --> 00:00:35.958
<b>Lord Krishna is explaining the distinction </b>
<b>between renunciation and Karma Yoga.</b>

3
00:00:35.958 --> 00:00:41.125
<b>He is making Arjuna understand the importance </b>
<b>of Karma Yoga being simple and practical.</b>

4
00:00:41.125 --> 00:00:45.583
<b>In this verse, Lord Krishna</b>
<b>says that without Karma Yoga,</b>

5
00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:48.708
<b>it is extremely difficult to attain renunciation.</b>

6
00:00:48.708 --> 00:00:53.500
<b>Without Karma Yoga, even if </b>
<b>one renounces all their actions,</b>

7
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:58.625
<b>they will neither attain happiness nor liberation.</b>

8
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:03.375


9
00:01:03.375 --> 00:01:05.208
<b>When you climb stairs,</b>

10
00:01:05.208 --> 00:01:06.750
<b>what do you do?</b>

11
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.166
<b>First on the first step,</b>

12
00:01:08.166 --> 00:01:09.291
<b>then the second,</b>

13
00:01:09.291 --> 00:01:10.333
<b>then the third.</b>

14
00:01:10.333 --> 00:01:14.208
<b>If after the first step, you directly </b>
<b>put your foot on the third,</b>

15
00:01:14.208 --> 00:01:18.250
<b>there is a likelihood of slipping and falling down.</b>

16
00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:19.333
<b>Similarly,</b>

17
00:01:19.333 --> 00:01:25.041
<b>when an attempt is made to attain </b>
<b>renunciation without the support of Karma Yoga,</b>

18
00:01:25.041 --> 00:01:28.541
<b>not only do many difficulties arise,</b>

19
00:01:28.541 --> 00:01:30.750
<b>but dissatisfaction also remains.</b>

20
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.125
<b>Our mind is so fickle,</b>

21
00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:35.458
<b>similarly our senses are</b>

22
00:01:35.458 --> 00:01:41.666
<b>always eager to get something, </b>
<b>to taste something or to see something.</b>

23
00:01:41.666 --> 00:01:45.666
<b>It is the nature of the mind and senses </b>
<b>to remain engaged in work.</b>

24
00:01:45.666 --> 00:01:51.500
<b>Until the mind and senses are focused </b>
<b>on some higher spiritual point,</b>

25
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:58.125
<b>the possibility of them running back </b>
<b>and forth and getting agitated always remains.</b>

26
00:01:58.125 --> 00:02:01.291
<b>This is why renunciation is difficult.</b>

27
00:02:01.291 --> 00:02:02.083
<b>But</b>

28
00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:07.541
<b>those who are engaged in Karma Yoga, </b>
<b>they remain active in this world,</b>

29
00:02:07.541 --> 00:02:11.333
<b>but due to non-attachment to </b>
<b>the results of their actions,</b>

30
00:02:11.333 --> 00:02:13.583
<b>they do not have dissatisfaction.</b>

31
00:02:13.583 --> 00:02:18.958
<b>Considering their action as their duty, they </b>
<b>are always engaged in their work,</b>

32
00:02:18.958 --> 00:02:23.833
<b>and certainly attain the highest position </b>
<b>and the Supreme Brahman.</b>

33
00:02:23.833 --> 00:02:25.791
<b>Lord Krishna is clarifying</b>

34
00:02:25.791 --> 00:02:31.000
<b>that when you renounce actions </b>
<b>without the support of Karma Yoga,</b>

35
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.000
<b>renunciation becomes extremely difficult</b>

36
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.500
<b>and therefore the possibility of misery increases.</b>

37
00:02:39.208 --> 00:02:43.333
<b>  </b>

38
00:02:43.333 --> 00:02:47.708
<b>Has it ever happened to you that,</b>

39
00:02:47.708 --> 00:02:50.500
<b>when faced with a challenge,</b>

40
00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:56.625
<b>or seeing a path full of thorns and stones ahead,</b>

41
00:02:56.625 --> 00:02:59.791
<b>you went in some other direction?</b>

42
00:02:59.791 --> 00:03:01.125
<b>And,</b>

43
00:03:01.125 --> 00:03:07.250
<b>did problems or challenges not </b>
<b>come in that other direction?</b>

44
00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:15.458
<b>In such a situation, where will you go?</b>
<b>Wherever you go, whichever path you choose,</b>

45
00:03:15.458 --> 00:03:21.125
<b>you will have to face obstacles and hurdles.</b>

46
00:03:21.125 --> 00:03:23.166
<b>While studying,</b>

47
00:03:23.166 --> 00:03:27.500
<b>when a student finds a subject difficult,</b>

48
00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:31.500
<b>they just stop studying it.</b>

49
00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:36.125
<b>At that moment, it seems </b>
<b>like they did the right thing.</b>

50
00:03:36.125 --> 00:03:41.041
<b>But after that,</b>

51
00:03:41.041 --> 00:03:46.333
<b>don't they have to face self-condemnation?</b>

52
00:03:46.333 --> 00:03:48.958
<b>And if that same student,</b>

53
00:03:48.958 --> 00:03:53.166
<b>without worrying about success </b>
<b>or failure in the exam,</b>

54
00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:56.041
<b>just studies their lesson,</b>

55
00:03:56.041 --> 00:04:00.416
<b>tries to understand it,</b>

56
00:04:00.416 --> 00:04:07.666
<b>then they start enjoying this </b>
<b>challenging process itself.</b>

57
00:04:07.666 --> 00:04:10.916
<b>Even if they get low marks in the exam,</b>

58
00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:18.791
<b>that situation is far superior to living in a state of self-condemnation.</b>

59
00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.083
<b>For this reason,</b>

60
00:04:20.083 --> 00:04:24.833
<b>whenever difficulties or challenges come in life,</b>

61
00:04:24.833 --> 00:04:28.750
<b>accept them with open arms.</b>

62
00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:34.041
<b>Without paying too much attention </b>
<b>to what the result will be,</b>

63
00:04:34.041 --> 00:04:40.000
<b>just face the challenges </b>
<b>head-on, stick to your actions.</b>

64
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.500
<b>And believe me,</b>

65
00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:51.666
<b>fulfilling your responsibility </b>
<b>is itself a very big reward.</b>

66
00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:56.250
<b> </b>

67
00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:59.166
<b>As you act,</b>

68
00:04:59.166 --> 00:05:02.333
<b>so you react.</b>

69
00:05:02.333 --> 00:05:06.958
<b>The velocity with which you throw a ball,</b>

70
00:05:06.958 --> 00:05:11.791
<b>it will come back with the same velocity.</b>

71
00:05:11.791 --> 00:05:14.458
<b>	Many times it happens</b>

72
00:05:14.458 --> 00:05:18.791
<b>that a family member is </b>
<b>frustrated or disappointed,</b>

73
00:05:18.791 --> 00:05:26.041
<b>in the heat of the moment they often </b>
<b>say inappropriate and harsh words.</b>

74
00:05:26.041 --> 00:05:28.500
<b>Then what do you do,</b>

75
00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:37.041
<b>say even harsher words in response, </b>
<b>or bear this harsh behavior</b>

76
00:05:37.041 --> 00:05:40.583
<b>and subdue its intensity.</b>

77
00:05:40.583 --> 00:05:46.958
<b>When harsh words are met with harsher words,</b>

78
00:05:46.958 --> 00:05:53.916
<b>there is a risk of relationships breaking.</b>

79
00:05:53.916 --> 00:05:56.083
<b>Through the Gita,</b>

80
00:05:56.083 --> 00:05:59.916
<b>I want to teach you</b>

81
00:05:59.916 --> 00:06:06.500
<b>that our true character is </b>
<b>tested only in difficult times.</b>

82
00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:11.458
<b>The very meaning of family relationships</b>

83
00:06:11.458 --> 00:06:16.000
<b>is to become such a shield for each other</b>

84
00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:22.875
<b>that can easily withstand the slaps of bad times.</b>

85
00:06:22.875 --> 00:06:32.208
<b>If ever a bad time or a family member's </b>
<b>harsh behavior comes in front in the family,</b>

86
00:06:32.208 --> 00:06:37.958
<b>do not do what seems right at that </b>
<b>moment by getting excited.</b>

87
00:06:37.958 --> 00:06:41.333
<b>Let a few moments pass with restraint,</b>

88
00:06:41.333 --> 00:06:46.000
<b>do not turn your face away </b>
<b>from the calamity either.</b>

89
00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:51.791
<b>Think about the far-reaching </b>
<b>consequences of your behavior.</b>

90
00:06:51.791 --> 00:06:53.541
<b>You will find that</b>

91
00:06:53.541 --> 00:07:00.625
<b>due to discretion, you are </b>
<b>becoming aware of your family duty.</b>

92
00:07:00.625 --> 00:07:07.750
<b>This is what will strengthen the </b>
<b>love between family members.</b>

93
00:07:09.208 --> 00:07:13.291



94
00:07:13.291 --> 00:07:17.875
<b>Two people make equal efforts,</b>

95
00:07:17.875 --> 00:07:21.708
<b>but one tastes success</b>

96
00:07:21.708 --> 00:07:25.375
<b>and the other fails.</b>

97
00:07:25.375 --> 00:07:30.791
<b>In the business world, there are many </b>
<b>reasons considered for success,</b>

98
00:07:30.791 --> 00:07:36.500
<b>such as hard work, complete </b>
<b>dedication and firmness.</b>

99
00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:37.750
<b>But</b>

100
00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:48.000
<b>if everyone does all that, then why </b>
<b>are everyone's results different?</b>

101
00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.583
<b>Because</b>

102
00:07:49.583 --> 00:07:56.000
<b>you give more importance </b>
<b>to the result than the effort.</b>

103
00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:00.458
<b>Hard work or firmness alone is not enough,</b>

104
00:08:00.458 --> 00:08:08.333
<b>knowledge also plays an important </b>
<b>role in your efforts along with it.</b>

105
00:08:08.333 --> 00:08:15.875
<b>When there is wisdom in the effort </b>
<b>instead of eagerness for the result,</b>

106
00:08:15.875 --> 00:08:18.791
<b>then there is also knowledge.</b>

107
00:08:18.791 --> 00:08:21.500
<b>Through the Gita,</b>

108
00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:26.375
<b>I want to tell you about the path</b>

109
00:08:26.375 --> 00:08:28.541
<b>on which, while walking,</b>

110
00:08:28.541 --> 00:08:35.750
<b>you will give more importance to your </b>
<b>actions than success and failure.</b>

111
00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:39.250
<b>Yes, you understood it right –</b>

112
00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:42.958
<b>selfless Karma Yoga.</b>

113
00:08:42.958 --> 00:08:44.458
<b>Suppose</b>

114
00:08:44.458 --> 00:08:49.333
<b>you are leading a very important project.</b>

115
00:08:49.333 --> 00:08:56.916
<b>Adhering to a tight deadline, </b>
<b>you throw yourself in completely.</b>

116
00:08:56.916 --> 00:09:01.166
<b>Your team of colleagues is also under pressure</b>

117
00:09:01.166 --> 00:09:06.000
<b>that they have to support you </b>
<b>with their highest performance.</b>

118
00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.041
<b>In such pressure,</b>

119
00:09:08.041 --> 00:09:12.625
<b>the possibility of mistakes always remains.</b>

120
00:09:12.625 --> 00:09:17.750
<b>In such a situation, </b>
<b>the deadline is met, but</b>

121
00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:23.791
<b>the precise goals of the project are often missed.</b>

122
00:09:23.791 --> 00:09:26.458
<b>Instead of doing this,</b>

123
00:09:26.458 --> 00:09:32.833
<b>if you make a process for your entire project.</b>

124
00:09:32.833 --> 00:09:42.541
<b>Keeping the timeline in mind, divide </b>
<b>the project objective into smaller goals.</b>

125
00:09:42.541 --> 00:09:48.083
<b>Anticipate challenges to prevent</b>
<b>mistakes from happening,</b>

126
00:09:48.083 --> 00:09:51.625
<b>and continuously assess the situation,</b>

127
00:09:51.625 --> 00:09:57.166
<b>then this type of leadership </b>
<b>style will be called thoughtful.</b>

128
00:09:57.166 --> 00:10:01.291
<b>And if the process is smooth,</b>

129
00:10:01.291 --> 00:10:06.958
<b>the probability of achieving the goals </b>
<b>will also increase manifold.</b>

130
00:10:06.958 --> 00:10:15.916
<b>This kind of process-centric approach</b>
<b>helps in long-term progress.</b>

131
00:10:15.916 --> 00:10:19.791
<b>Selfless Karma Yoga requires –</b>

132
00:10:19.791 --> 00:10:21.166
<b>firmness</b>

133
00:10:21.166 --> 00:10:22.333
<b>and</b>

134
00:10:22.333 --> 00:10:25.833
<b>the wisdom of a sage.</b>

135
00:10:25.833 --> 00:10:32.833
<b>Where you take the second </b>
<b>step only after taking the first step.</b>

136
00:10:32.833 --> 00:10:37.750
<b>This can prove to be a path</b>

137
00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:42.250
<b>where while fulfilling your professional goals,</b>

138
00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:51.166
<b>you will also emerge as a hardworking </b>
<b>and inspiring leader for your team.</b>

